The "overlap" on X is `(ball.r + brick.w/2) - absDiffX`.
The "overlap" on Y is `(ball.r + brick.h/2) - absDiffY`.

If overlapX < overlapY, it's a side hit.
If overlapY < overlapX, it's a top/bottom hit.

